BE papersofulyssess0012gran '"visits Orange Court House"' 1 [{"text": ["A man employed by the Provost Marshal {{{visits Orange Court House}}} regularly and gets accurate reports from"]}]
BE papersofulyssess0012gran '"Wednesday last"' 0 []
BE papersofulyssess0012gran '"Orange Court House" Early' 1 [{"text": ["Potomac and {{{Early}}} to advance at the same time from Martinsburg\u2014this was frustrated by {{{Early}}} being compelled", "Sheridan in the pursuit of {{{Early}}}. I thought it possible though not probable that {{{Early}}} might turn North or send", "you I would not say this {{{early}}} did were it not that any move should be made {{{early}}}\u201d ALS (telegram sent),", "Berryville reports {{{Early}}}, (or Longstreet, I do not yet know which is in command, but think {{{Early}}} is) with the", " 22. Sheridan again defeated Lt. Gen. Jubal A. {{{Early}}} at the battle of Fisher\u2019s Hill, Va.\nSEPT. 24. USG"]}]
BE papersofulyssess0012gran 'Leet Bowers August' 0 []
BE papersofulyssess0012gran '"badly whipped"' 1 [{"text": ["attacked us at Reams Station last night and were {{{badly whipped}}}\u2014\u2019 Have you any information of it? Please answer\u201d", "to attack the enemy before night\u2014Early was {{{badly whipped}}} yesterday\u2014Have not yet received full reports\u2014The"]}]
BE papersofulyssess0012gran '"Fitzhugh Lee"' 0 []
BE papersofulyssess0012gran '"gets accurate reports from"' 1 [{"text": ["visits Orange Court House regularly and {{{gets accurate reports from}}} there. Not a regiment has passed there"]}]
BE papersofulyssess0012gran '"employed by the Provost Marshal"' 1 [{"text": ["know have gone to the valley. A man {{{employed by the Provost Marshal}}} visits Orange Court House regularly"]}]
BE papersofulyssess0012gran '"Orange Court House" Sharpe' 1 [{"text": ["Army), 80n, 89n, 95n, 99n, 126n\n{{{Sharpe}}}, Alexander B. (U.S. Army), 436\n{{{Sharpe}}}, George H. (N.Y. Vols.), 1697", "man employed by the Provost Marshal visits {{{Orange Court House}}} regularly and gets accurate reports from", "was making a great flank movement and today Col {{{Sharpe}}} sends information (despatch transmitted) that the", "is in O.R.., I, xlii, part 2, 967.\n1. George H. {{{Sharpe}}}, born in 1828 in Kingston, N. Y., graduated from", "Army of the Potomac, by Maj. Gen. Joseph Hooker, {{{Sharpe}}} retained that position through the war. See ibid"]}]
BE papersofulyssess0012gran '"Fitz Lee"' 1 [{"text": ["Fort Lafayette\u2014They are both named {{{Fitz Lee}}} but one is known as {{{Fitz Lee}}} & the other as Rooney Lee among", "AucusT 16, 1864 9\n(\u2014\u2018Rooney\u2019 Lee) \u2014Gen Lees son not {{{Fitz Lee}}} who is the oldest Division Com- mander but the", "WASHINGTON,\nIt is understood in Richmond that {{{Fitz Lee}}} has been ordered back from the valley with his", "you that I had good reason for believing that {{{Fitz Lee}}} had been ordered back here? I now think it likely", "Lomax is in command of the Valley Cavalry, and {{{Fitz Lee}}} in command of all Cavalry in the Valley. Breckenridge\u2019s"]}]
